[24.6095, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m \u001b[2mgrip is reading your diff…\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[24.6101, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2mrefund() gains an idempotency key: a retried refund returns the existing refund id instead of \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mcharging the gateway twice, and the balance check now reports the remaining amount.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[24.6108, "o", "\u001b[2mAnswer in a sentence or two. Press Enter on an empty line to skip.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[24.6113, "o", "\u001b[1;36mQ1/5\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(behaviour)\u001b[0m What happens now when refund() is called twice with the same idempotency key?\r\n"]
